ps for uric acid and 100 strips for cholesterol (with expiry date at least 1 yr from delivery) (strips available at local drugstores nationwide)\r\n2. 1 Lancing Device\r\n3. 150 Lancets\r\n4. 1 Carrying case\r\nG. Bag Valve Mask (adult and pedia)- 1 set\r\n- Autoclavable\r\n- ADULT: 1.5L bag, with pressure relief valve (60cmH20), size 5 mask\r\nWith 2pcs face mask, 3pcs oral airway, reservoir bag and oxygen tubing \r\n- PEDIATRIC: 550ml bag with pressure relief valve (40cmH20), size 3 mask\r\n- With 2pcs face mask, 3pcs oral airway, reservoir bag and oxygen tubing\r\nH. Digital medical tape measure- 1 unit\r\n- easy to use, compact design\r\n- measures up to 9 different body parts\r\n- measurement units: inches and cm\r\n- Stores previous measurements \r\n- 80 inch / 190cm extendable tape\r\n- 2 measuring Mode: circumferences and linear mode\r\n- Bright LCD digital display\r\n- batteries required\r\n- With free battery/ies and battery charger\r\nI. Pen light- 1 set\r\n- 2 pcs penlights (white & yellow light)\r\nmade of alluminum alloy\r\n- With push button on/off switch\r\n- Powered by two (2) AAA batteries\r\n- with pupil gauge\r\n- Dimensions: 5\" long in diameter\r\nJ. Fetal Doppler, portable- 1 unit\r\nFeatures and Specifications:\r\nHigh Sensitivity water proof probes: 2MHz and 3MHz, (Interchangeable)\r\nLarge backlit LCD display (at least 25x45mm)\r\nFHR detection with high fidelity sound\r\nBuilt-in audio recorder\r\nRechargeable Battery: Lithium Polymer\r\nAuto shut-off\r\nFHR Range: 30-240bpm\r\nAlarm Sound Speaker: Built-in loud speaker with volume control\r\nStandard Accessories:\r\nAC Adapter (Auto volt)\r\nWith carrying case\r\nK. Multifunctional Percussion Diagnostic Reflex Percussion Hammer Set- 1 set\r\nMaterial: Medical grade stainless steel and rubber\r\nsize: 20x5.1cm\r\ncolor: mint/apple green \r\nconsists of: 1. Pinwheel / Geer Wheel Hammer\r\n2. T-shape Hammer / Triple-cornered Hammer\r\n3. Taylor Buck Hammer\r\n4. Babinski Hammer / Metal Rod Hammer\r\n5. Plastic Rod Hammer\r\nL. ENT Diagnostic Set (Ophthalmoscope, Otoscope) - 1 set\r\nBayonet locking, mounts to the battery handle\r\nWith rechargeable batteries and charger\r\nChrome plated battery handle with knurled finish\r\nRheostatic on/off switch\r\n5 specula, size 2.75mm\r\n5 specula, size 4.25mm\r\nOtoscope\r\nChrome-plated otoscope head with removable 4x magnifying lens, and insufflator fitting\r\nAdapter to allow use with disposable specula\r\nNasal speculum adapter with manual screw opening for instrumentation connects to the otoscope head\r\nOphthalmoscope Head \r\nWith lens wheel featuring 25 corrective lenses from 25 to +40 diopters\r\nM. Salter Scale (50kg capacity)- 1 unit\r\nHeavy Duty, hanging\r\nWith 2 pcs. Hanging Hooks and baby hanging trousers\r\nLarge easy to read dial display with white background\r\nCapacity: 25 kg x 50kgs\r\nResolution: 0.1 kg\r\nAccuracy: 0.1%\r\nNet Weight: atleast 800 gms\r\nN. Digital Weighing Scale for newborn, portable\r\nWeight: not more than 3 kgs\r\nDisplay Type: Digital\r\nMaximum weight: 20 kgs\r\nGradation: 5g\r\nType: Portable \r\nWith BMIF function (Breast-Milk-Intake Function)\r\nBabies can be weighed in a lying and or sitting position\r\nO. Pulse Oximeter (finger type)- 1 unit\r\nSpO2: measurement range: 35-100%\r\naccuracy: ± 2%\r\nresolution: 1%\r\nPulse Rate: Measurement range : 30-250 bpm\r\nAccuracy: ± 2bpm\r\nResolution: 1bpm\r\nAlarm Function: Audible and visual alarms for high/low SpO2 and PR\r\nWith Low Signal Quality Alarm, & Low battery indicator\r\nPower requirements: Compatible with lithium batteries and standard \"AAA\" size batteries IPX2 Dimensions: Manufacturer\'s dimensions\r\nAccessories:\r\nBackpack\r\nCapacity: not less than 29L \r\nMaterials: 100% Polyester; Water resistant and lightweight\r\nDimensions: 18.5\"(H) x 13\"(W) x 7.5\"(D)\r\nColor: Mint Green\r\nWith laser printed DOH logo (front) 6 inches and DOH-CAR (HFEP) letters- 2 inches\r\n'),
(35, 19, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 100000.00000, 22.00, NULL, NULL, 30, 'Medical Furniture Package\r\nA. Mechanical Bed 2 cranks (1 unit)\r\n2 cranks for angle adjustment of head and foot end\r\nStainless steel frame with ABS Sectioned support mattress\r\nDetachable head and foot board (ABS material)\r\nFunctions:\r\nBackrest Upwards: can be adjusted up to 75°\r\nKnee-rest Upwards: can be adjusted up to 40°\r\nGuard Rails: Fold-away aluminum side rails\r\nCastors: With wheels; with brakes\r\nMattress: Rubberized, at least 4 in thick with water resistant cover\r\nDining Table: Provided with fold~away dining table (folds towards footboard)\r\nIV Stand: Detachable, Tubular, With at least 2 hooks\r\nFoot Stool: One (1) single step powder coated steel; with non-slip rubber padding\r\nLWH 51x30x23cm (+/-3cm)\r\nAll joints, fittings shall be free from burrs or rough edges\r\nAll permanent joints and braces shall be full-weld\r\nB. Medical Cabinet (1 unit)\r\nStandard Features:\r\nStainless steel sheet with two side glass, two glass doors with lock\r\nThree glass shelves (adjustable)\r\nWith a base compartment with two stainless steel doors, one shelf with lock mounted on heavy duty rubber castors with lock\r\n18” W x 36” L x 72” H (± 2”)\r\nAll joints, fittings shall be free from burrs or rough edges -\r\nC. IV Stand (1 unit)\r\nAdjustable height, with at least 3 hooks\r\nStainless steel and ABS material\r\nTelescopic stainless-steel rod, adjustable up to at least 72in\r\nLocking hand wheel mounted on at least 24in, 4~legged aluminum base with swivel casters\r\nD. Examination Lamp (1 unit)\r\nStainless steel and ABS material\r\nLED bulb ≥7W\r\nLamp head with flexible neck for multiple adjustment/position\r\nPower supply: (220-230V AC)\r\nAdjustable height\r\nStable base with at least 5-50mm castors -\r\nE. Bedside Table- (1 unit)\r\nTechnical Specifications:\r\n480x480x760 (+/-30mm)\r\nMade of Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene (ABS) material\r\nWith cabinet and 2 shelves\r\nWith 2 pull out drawers\r\nWith rack on each side\r\nWith accessory hooks\r\nWith castors; lock/brake\r\nAll joints and fittings shall be free from rough edges\r\nF. Delivery Table- (1 unit)\r\nStainless steel. Dimensions: 72 x 22 x 30 inches (L x W x H) +/- 3 inches\r\nWith height adjustable padded stirrups (removable) Adjustable back rest angle. Adjustable leg rest angle (downwards towards floor) \r\nWith side grab handles Matress-3-sections ruberrized, 3 inches thick\r\n with washable water-resistant cover with stainless steel (rotating, height adjustable) stool and foot stool \r\nwith non-slip rubber base \r\nWith stainless steel bucket and bucket holder. \r\nWith IV pole- 2 hooks\r\nStandard Requirements: (to be submitted during post qualification)\r\n1. Product brochure or technical data sheet(s) of the equipment showing the technical specifications in English language.\r\n2. Valid and current Certificate of Compliance of manufacturer of the equipment with the latest version of ISO 13485: Quality Management System - Requirements for regulatory purposes in the name of the manufacturer. The Certificates must be issued by an independent Certifying Body/Agency.\r\n3. Valid Certificate of Distributorship (as first Tier Distributor) issued by the Manufacturer of each equipment authorizing the bidder to sell/distribute the offered equipment.\r\n4.  Proof (such as sales invoice) that the Brand of the equipment has been sold to other health facilities in the Philippines.\r\n5.  Bidder\'s valid and current License to Operate (LTO) as a medical device distributor issued by the Philippine Food and Drug Administration. In case of expired LTO, the following must be submitted: i) Copy of expired LTO, ii) Application for renewal, iii) Official Receipt as proof of payment for the renewal of LTO\r\n6. Notarized Certificate from the bidder:\r\na)      That the brand of the equipment has been in the local and/or international market for at least 3 years.\r\nb)     That the equipment and its accessories are brand new, unused, not discontinued models and were not subjected to any product recall. Equipment model must not be more than 3 years old.\r\nb)     That the equipment and its accessories are brand new, unused, not discontinued models and were not subjected to any product recall. Equipment model must not be more than 3 years old.\r\nc) That the supplier shall, a. Either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. b. Within the warranty period, shall conduct a preventive maintenance on the equipment at least every six months or according to the manufacturer\'s recommendations on the schedule of preventive maintenance c. Conduct necessary corrective maintenance within fourteen calendar days (14) upon notification from end-user regarding equipment breakdown/defect. d. The supplier shall have responsibilities and accountabilities that upon evaluation of equipment defects/faults, the equipment is appropriately repaired/replaced and shall be in good working condition thereafter. e. The number of days where the equipment is unusable due to equipment faults/defects shall be added to the warranty period. f. Supplier shall post warranty comprehensive preventive maintenance costs including list and prices of major spare parts of the equipment for the next three (3) years after the warranty period.\r\n7. Valid Marketing Authorization, Registration Approval or Free Sale Certificate for the Automatic External Defibrillator issued by the Health Authority in the country of origin. (as applicable)\r\nRequirements if awarded the Contract\r\n1. Completion period: The delivery and installation of the equipment and its accessories, shall be completed within 45 calendar days from receipt of Notice to Proceed.\r\n2. Testing/ Commissioning:  Prior to acceptance, the end user shall conduct a physical inspection and functionality test. The equipment must be functioning and must have no physical damage and defect.\r\n3. Training: The supplier shall provide an orientation/ training and certificate of completion on the proper use and maintenance of the equipment to the end-users upon delivery or on agreed date of training\r\n4.       Warranty: Warranty certificate for two (2) year on parts and on services. The supplier shall either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. The warranty period shall commence from the date of acceptance by the end-user after testing and commissioning.\r\n4.       Warranty: Warranty certificate for two (2) year on parts and on services. The supplier shall either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. The warranty period shall commence from the date of acceptance by the end-user after testing and commissioning.\r\n5. The supplier must provide the Operations Manual in English language to the end-­user.\r\n6. With DOH-CHD-CAR (HFEP) letters, with appropriate size, laser printed unto an appropriate visible area of the equipment/instrument.  For larger equipment, DOH-CHD-CAR (HFEP) letters at least 2 inches in height, laser printed unto an appropriate visible area of the equipment plus sticker containing among others, Year of the delivery of item, name of supplier and contact number of suppliers\r\n'),
