nical data sheet(s) of the equipment showing the technical specifications in English language.\r\n2. Valid and current Certificate of Compliance of manufacturer of the equipment with the latest version of ISO 13485: Quality Management System - Requirements for regulatory purposes in the name of the manufacturer. The Certificates must be issued by an independent Certifying Body/Agency.\r\n3. Valid Certificate of Distributorship (as first Tier Distributor) issued by the Manufacturer of each equipment authorizing the bidder to sell/distribute the offered equipment.\r\n4.  Proof (such as sales invoice) that the Brand of the equipment has been sold to other health facilities in the Philippines.\r\n5.  Bidder\'s valid and current License to Operate (LTO) as a medical device distributor issued by the Philippine Food and Drug Administration. In case of expired LTO, the following must be submitted: i) Copy of expired LTO, ii) Application for renewal, iii) Official Receipt as proof of payment for the renewal of LTO\r\n6. Notarized Certificate from the bidder:\r\na) That the brand of the equipment has been in the local and/or international market for at least 3 years.\r\nb)That the equipment and its accessories are brand new, unused, not discontinued models and were not subjected to any product recall. Equipment model must not be more than 3 years old.\r\nc) That the supplier shall, a. Either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. b. Within the warranty period, shall conduct a preventive maintenance on the equipment at least every six months or according to the manufacturer\'s recommendations on the schedule of preventive maintenance c. Conduct necessary corrective maintenance within fourteen calendar days (14) upon notification from end-user regarding equipment breakdown/defect. \r\nd. The supplier shall have responsibilities and accountabilities that upon evaluation of equipment defects/faults, the equipment are appropriately repaired/replaced and shall be in good working condition thereafter. \r\ne. The number of days where the equipment is unusable due to equipment faults/defects shall be added to the warranty period.\r\nf. Supplier shall post warranty comprehensive preventive maintenance costs including list and prices of major spare parts of the equipment for the next three (3) years after the warranty period.\r\n7. Valid Marketing Authorization, Registration Approval or Free Sale Certificate for the Automatic External Defibrillator issued by the Health Authority in the country of origin. (as applicable)\r\nRequirements if awarded the Contract\r\n1. Completion period: The delivery and installation of the equipment and its accessories, shall be completed within 30 working days from receipt of Notice to Proceed.\r\n2. Testing/ Commissioning:  Prior to acceptance, the end user shall conduct a physical inspection and functionality test. The equipment must be functioning and must have no physical damage and defect.\r\n3. Training: The supplier shall provide an orientation/ training and certificate of completion on the proper use and maintenance of the equipment to the end-users upon delivery or on agreed date of training\r\n4. Warranty: Warranty certificate for two (2) year on parts and on services. The supplier shall either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. The warranty period shall commence from the date of acceptance by the end-user after testing and commissioning.\r\n5. The supplier must provide the Operations Manual in English language to the end-­user.\r\n6. With DOH-CHD-CAR (HFEP) letters, with appropriate size, laser printed unto an appropriate visible area of the equipment/instrument.  For larger equipment, DOH-CHD-CAR (HFEP) letters at least 2 inches in height, laser printed unto an appropriate visible area of the equipment plus sticker containing among others, Year of the delivery of item, name of supplier and contact number of supplier\r\n'),
