Administration. In case of expired LTO, the following must be submitted: i) Copy of expired LTO, ii) Application for renewal, iii) Official Receipt as proof of payment for the renewal of LTO\n6. Notarized Certificate from the bidder:\na)      That the brand of the equipment has been in the local and/or international market for at least 3 years.\nb)     That the equipment and its accessories are brand new, unused, not discontinued models and were not \nsubjected to any product recall. Equipment model must not be more than 3 years old.\nc) That the supplier shall, a. Either repair or replace any item or part in the equipment that is found to be defective in material or in workmanship under normal use. \nb. Within the warranty period, shall conduct a preventive maintenance on the equipment at least every six months or according to the manufacturer\'s recommendations on the schedule of preventive maintenance c. Conduct necessary corrective maintenance within fourteen calendar days (14) upon notification from end-user regarding equipment breakdown/defect. d. The supplier shall have responsibilities and accountabilities that upon evaluation of equipment defects/faults, the equipment is appropriately repaired/replaced and shall be in good working condition thereafter. e. The number of days where the equipment is unusable due to equipment faults/defects shall be added to the warranty period. f. Supplier shall post warranty comprehensive preventive maintenance costs including list and prices of major spare parts of the equipment for the next three (3) years after the warranty period.\n7. Valid Marketing Authorization, Registration Approval or Free Sale Certificate for the Automatic External Defibrillator issued by the Health Authority in the country of origin. (as applicable)'),
