(652, 305, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1680.00000, 150.00, NULL, NULL, 12, 'HYGIENE KIT CONTENTS:\na.) Utility Pail, plastic, at least 16 liters capacity, with lockable cover that serves as a basin and secured with two pieces cable tie, color green, with heavy duty metal handle, with DOH Logo 6\"x6\"\nb.) Dipper, plastic, diameter- 6 inches, height- 4.5 inches, with straight handle, colored, 1 piece per kit\nc.) Tooth paste, with maximum fluoride/cavity protection, minimum 145 grams per tube, individually packed/box, 1 tube per kit\nd.) Toothbrush for adult, with plastic case for the brush bristle, soft/ medium bristle, not intended for one time use or non- disposable , individually packed in blister, 3 pcs per kit\n\"e.) Toothbrush for Children, with plastic case for the brush bristle, soft bristle, not intended for one-time use or non-disposable, individually packed in blister, 2pcs per kit\"\nf.) Shampoo with conditioner, mild scented,12 ml per sachet, 5 sachets per plastic pack\nh.) Laundry/Detergent soap, minimum of 380 grams, white, individually packed with plastic, 2 bars per kit\ni.) 2 tissue rolls 2-ply;\nj.) Sanitary napkin/pad, regular non-wings, with adhesive, individually wrapped, 8 pads per pack, 4 packs per kit\nk.) Hand Towel, rectangular shape, dark colored, 100% cotton, length - 43 - 50 cm ; width- 27 cm ; sewed edge, 5 pieces per plastic pack, 1 plastic pack per kit\nl.) Bath Towel, 100% cotton, typical size around 30x54 inches, individually packed, 1 piece per kit, dark colored\nm.) Malong, individually packed, standard size: width-40 inches; length- at least 58 inches Material: cotton, 1 piece per kit\nn.) Undergarments, 100% cotton, plain colored, 12 pcs per pack: - 6 pieces in a pack for men (2pcs-Small, 2pcs medium, 2pcs-large)\n- 6 pieces in a pack for women (2pcs-Small, 2pcs medium, 2pcs-large)\no.) Plastic Comb, 1 piece, at least 14 cm in length\np.) Nail Cutter, 1 piece, at least 5cm, carbon steel\nq.) 1 pack diaper, 4 pcs per pack, size large\nr.) 2 Slippers size 7 and 8\ns.) Chamber pot, plastic, medium- sized'),
(653, 305, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 9980.00000, 7.00, NULL, NULL, 17, 'Trauma Bag Emergency Medical Trauma Bag- Color: Red, Overall dimensions: 20\"(L)x16\"(W)x10(H), Front & Side Pockets Stretch Full-Length of Bag + Feature Interior Elastic Instrument Loops and Nylon Pockets w/ dividers; each colored quick access pouch includes Clear Vinyl Window & Interior Pocket; has elastic loops for securing bottles/cylindrical items, Main Flap is padded and Features three clear zippered  Compartments for Access to often used items without disturbing main-hold supplies; Silver triple trim reflective stripping surrounds bag + 3M Scotch lite Stitched into webbing and straps, raised PVC/Nylon reinforcement Covers Bottom and Lower half of Bag for water and Abrasion Resistance. With reinforced Nylon handle and metal buckle for anchoring of padded shoulder strap\nMinor Wound Suturing Set: Content- Needle Holder (stainless Steel), Tissue Scissor (Stainless Steel), Tissue Forcep (stainless Steel), Eye Surgical towel, autoclavable material\nAsepto Irrigation Bulb Syringe 50 cc (plastic), graduated measurements, push handles for easy push of content, Materials: 1 pc per pouch, disposable\ntweezers stainless; long needle like tip, triangular tip, 3 - 4 \"\nSurvival Blanket, 160x210 cm, lightweight flexible wrap around blanket, easy to fold, strong and tear resistant, Material: non-stretch polyester film, wind, water and rot proof\n\nSTANDARD REQUIREMENTS\n1. Shelf life: With a total shelf life of 24 months but not less than 18 months from the date of delivery.\n2. PACKAGING: Standard packaging of the manufacturer\nLABELLING INSTRUCTION: \na. On each box, the following should be permanently imprinted:\nPhilippine Government Property-Department of Health\nNOT FOR SALE\nb. The items should be delivered in a thick corrugated cardboard box, which is labeled in permanent black ink as follows, in addition to Recipient and Supplier:\nPhilippine Government Property-Department of Health NOT FOR SALE\nDate of Manufacture: ____________________\nDate of Expiry: _________________________\nBatch/Lot No. __________________________\n4. RECALL AND DISPOSAL:\na.) The supplier must ensure the quality products and if there will be problems in the quality, the supplier will recall and replace the products distributed in the hospitals/treatment hubs/RHU/HC/BHSs based on the Guidelines of Product Recall, FDA Circular No. 2016-12\nb.) In case of product recalls, damage or expired medicines due to replacement, costs associated with the proper handling or pull out from the health facilities where the goods have already been distributed shall be borne by the supplier\nADDITIONAL TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS (to be submitted during Post Qualification by the bidder with the Single/Lowest Calculated Bid)\n1. Valid PFDA Certificate of Product Registration (CPR) or Valid Extension issued by Philippine Food and Drugs Administration (PFDA); \nThe CPR must be valid for the entire period of award. If the CPR is about to expire, the supplier must have submitted a copy of an application of renewal to the FDA at least 3 months before the expiry date (a copy of the expiring CPR which is stamped with an Extension of Validity shall be submitted as proof); (AO 2019-0041)\n2. Valid and current License to Operate (LTO) issued by Philippine Food and Drugs Administration (PFDA). Provided, that the application for renewal was made timely as per DOH AO No. 2016-003:\n3. Product Insert/ Product Information \n4. Certificate of Good Manufacturing Practice from FDA (COA Circular No. 2024-010 dated July 31, 2024);\n5. Batch Release Certificate from FDA\n6. The bidder shall submit any of the following whichever is applicable:\na.) If the bidder is a manufacturer, certificate of the bidder manufactures the product/ items;\nb.) If the bidder is an Exclusive/ Authorized Distributor or Dealer of the products/items, Certificate of Contract from the manufacturer or importer must be provided as proof that the bidder is an Exclusive/ Authorized Distributor or dealer of the products/ items; or\nc.) If the bidder is an agent of the exclusive distributor or dealer, the following must be provided:\ni. Certificate or Distributor/ Dealership Agreement by the Manufacturer with the distributor or dealer; and\nii. Certification or Contract/ Dealership Agreement between the distributor/ dealer and the bidder.\n7. Certificate of Compliance to the Electronic Drug Price Monitoring System (EDPMS) issued by the Pharmaceutical Division (PD) of the DOH pursuant to DOH AO No. 2018-0020.'),
